Fix "Connect to Shopify" unreachable behind a reverse proxy/tunnel (v0.115)

ShopifySync.tsx built the OAuth start link by hitting the backend's own
port directly with a hardcoded ":8080" (window.location.hostname + ":8080"),
bypassing nginx's /api/ proxy that every other request in the app goes
through. That only ever worked on a bare LAN where both the frontend and
API ports are separately, directly reachable from the browser - behind a
reverse proxy, Cloudflare Tunnel, or a custom domain (e.g. a home server
exposed as wms.dan-cheetham.uk), the raw API port typically isn't exposed
externally at all, so the browser failed with "this site can't be reached"
before the app ever got a chance to respond, even though credentials and
everything else were configured correctly.

ShopifyOAuthController had a second, separate bug in the same area:
frontendUrl() (used for the post-callback landing redirect) hardcoded
":8081" for the frontend's port, which silently broke the moment v0.107
made that port configurable via FRONTEND_PORT.

Fix: both /start and /callback now go through the same origin as every
other API call (relative /api/shopify/oauth/start via nginx, instead of a
separate hardcoded port), and resolve the correct EXTERNAL base URL the
same way PasswordResetService already does for password-reset emails -
Settings > Email > "Public URL" (app_public_url) wins when set, since
request.getScheme() reports "http" even for HTTPS traffic arriving through
a reverse proxy (nginx.conf doesn't forward X-Forwarded-Proto), falling
back to guessing from the request only when Public URL is left blank
(correct for a bare LAN deployment, where the guess matches reality).
frontendUrl() as a separate method is gone entirely - callback and start
now share one resolvedBaseUrl() helper, since they're the same origin.

Settings.tsx's Public URL field description updated to mention it now also
drives the Shopify OAuth redirect, not just password-reset emails.

Practical note for deployments behind a custom domain/tunnel: Public URL
must be set for this to work, and if it's new or changes, the matching
redirect URL registered in the Shopify app's own settings needs updating to
match exactly (Shopify requires an exact match).

